        "One continuous five-second shot up a narrow stepped alley in the old medina of Chefchaouen, Morocco. Hand-plastered walls in layered indigo, cobalt and pale sky blue show chalky texture and small chips; worn stone steps climb to a central arched deep-blue wooden door beneath a small iron lantern, with terracotta pots of red geraniums on both sides. From the first frame the camera climbs the stairs in a fast, steady rising glide, near pots and wall corners sweeping past the frame edges with strong parallax as the door grows from distant to filling the center. A gust whips the white cotton curtain beside the door high and outward in a billowing arc, loose red petals tumbling down the steps. Warm sun rakes the upper wall, cool shade below. No people, no readable text, crisp stable architecture.",
